10. SYSTEM C — CARESENSE INTELLIGENT ASSISTANT
==================================================

THIS IS THE CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE COMPONENT.

Build a genuine context-aware decision engine.

Do not build a static chatbot that merely returns fixed answers.

Use deterministic, explainable JavaScript business rules.

The engine must analyse:

- Medication schedules.
- Medication status.
- Current time.
- Previous medication records.
- Upcoming appointments.
- Appointment changes.
- Caregiver activity.
- Notification preferences.
- Member permissions.
- Time zone.
- Recorded care routines.

Every generated recommendation or alert must contain:

1. What happened.
2. Why the system detected it.
3. Which records were relevant.
4. Who should be informed.
5. What action is appropriate.

DECISION SCENARIOS:

A. UPCOMING MEDICATION

Detect a medication approaching its scheduled time.

Show:
- Medication name.
- Scheduled time.
- Relevant instructions.
- Reminder status.

B. DUE MEDICATION

If a scheduled dose reaches its due time without confirmation:

- Display a due reminder.
- Identify the unconfirmed status.
- Avoid assuming the user did not take it.

C. OVERDUE MEDICATION

If the configured reminder window passes:

- Generate a caregiver attention alert.
- Explain the schedule and elapsed time.
- Queue an appropriate notification if enabled.

Use the wording "not yet confirmed" rather than automatically claiming the medication was missed.

D. MEDICATION MARKED TAKEN

- Update medication status.
- Record who updated it.
- Update adherence statistics.
- Update the shared timeline.
- Recalculate outstanding reminders.

E. MEDICATION MARKED SKIPPED

- Record the event.
- Flag it for appropriate review.
- Notify authorized members according to preferences.
- Never recommend an additional dose.

F. REPEATED UNCONFIRMED ENTRIES

Identify patterns across historical records.

- Explain the number of relevant records.
- Identify the dates involved.
- Suggest a caregiver check-in.
- Do not diagnose or predict medical emergencies.

G. UPCOMING APPOINTMENT

Detect appointments approaching their reminder window.

- Generate reminders.
- Show appointment details.
- Inform authorized recipients.
- Prevent duplicate notifications.

H. RESCHEDULED APPOINTMENT

- Update the shared calendar.
- Cancel obsolete pending reminders.
- Generate new reminders.
- Record the change.

I. CAREGIVER HANDOVER

When a caregiver records a handover:

- Preserve the previous notes.
- Record the new note.
- Identify the author.
- Update the shared activity timeline.

J. NOTIFICATION PREFERENCES

Only notify recipients who have appropriate permissions and have opted into the relevant notification category.

IMPORTANT:

CareSense must produce different decisions when its context changes.

It must not merely display prewritten messages.

Provide a transparent decision log.

Never claim machine learning or AI integration that does not exist.

